,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":198.181278058,"data":"[09:29:19]   [A 1/47] DAPT01EVAL-001 JAIN_TERMINOLOGY (192 tok) 'Ahimsa is defined as the avoidance of all forms of violence, including physical, verbal, mental, and emotional'\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":229.530151714,"data":"[09:29:51]   [A 2/47] DAPT01EVAL-002 JAIN_TERMINOLOGY (192 tok) \"According to Stevenson's Notes on Modern Jainism, Karma is a force that binds souls to the material world, pre\"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":260.607313472,"data":"[09:30:22]   [A 3/47] DAPT01EVAL-003 JAIN_TERMINOLOGY (192 tok) 'Stevenson identifies the two great divisions of Jain cosmic time as the *Kalpa* and the *Akalpa*. The *Kalpa* '\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":291.849762064,"data":"[09:30:53]   [A 4/47] DAPT01EVAL-004 JAIN_TERMINOLOGY (192 tok) 'According to Stevenson, the Three Jewels (Ratna Traya) in Jainism consist of the Jina (Tirthankara), the Sthav'\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":322.9858515,"data":"[09:31:24]   [A 5/47] DAPT01EVAL-005 STHANAKAVASI_TERMINOLOGY (192 tok) 'According to Stevenson, the Samayika is generally said by Sthanakavasi Jaina in the temple. However, it is als'\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":354.165654742,"data":"[09:31:55]   [A 6/47] DAPT01EVAL-006 STHANAKAVASI_TERMINOLOGY (192 tok) \"Stevenson's account of the Sthanakavasi canon lists 16 Mulagrantha. These are the same as the 16 Agamas, excep\"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":385.328980022,"data":"[09:32:27]   [A 7/47] DAPT01EVAL-007 STHANAKAVASI_TERMINOLOGY (192 tok) 'Vaiyavacca is a Jain term for the state of being in a state of impurity, which can be caused by physical conta'\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":416.455557717,"data":"[09:32:58]   [A 8/47] DAPT01EVAL-008 STHANAKAVASI_TERMINOLOGY (192 tok) 'According to Stevenson, the Terapanthi accept the Sthaviravadaniya and the Sthaviravadaniya Purva. They reject'\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":447.593016376,"data":"[09:33:29]   [A 9/47] DAPT01EVAL-009 PRAKRIT (192 tok) \"पाइय-सद्द-महान्नवो के अनुसार 'अहिंसण' शब्द का अर्थ है 'अहिंसा' या 'अहिंसा का अनुष्ठान'। यह शब्द जैन दर्शन के अ\"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":478.442072374,"data":"[09:34:00]   [A 10/47] DAPT01EVAL-010 PRAKRIT (192 tok) \"पाइय-सद्द-महान्नवो में प्राकृत शब्द 'उवस्सय' के लिए जैन शब्दकोष में दिया गया है 'उपस्थापन' या 'उपस्थिति'। यह श\"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":509.340698103,"data":"[09:34:31]   [A 11/47] DAPT01EVAL-011 PRAKRIT (192 tok) \"पाइय-सद्द-महान्नवो में प्राकृत शब्द 'सामइगि' का हिंदी रूप 'सामायिक' दिया गया है, जिसका अर्थ है 'साधु का एक आचा\"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":540.553751753,"data":"[09:35:02]   [A 12/47] DAPT01EVAL-012 PRAKRIT (192 tok) \"Woolner regarded Ardha Magadhi as the 'Prakrt par excellence'. He considered it the most archaic Prakrit, with\"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":571.838962435,"data":"[09:35:33]   [A 13/47] DAPT01EVAL-013 HINDI (192 tok) 'उत्तराध्ययन सूत्र की रचना भगवान महावीर के अंतिम उपदेश के रूप में हुई थी। इसका अधिकारी भगवान महावीर थे और इसका '\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":603.087481457,"data":"[09:36:04]   [A 14/47] DAPT01EVAL-014 HINDI (192 tok) 'उत्तराध्ययन शब्द का शाब्दिक अर्थ अध्ययन का उत्तर देना है। इसका अर्थ है कि जिस विषय का अध्ययन किया गया हो, उसके'\n"}
